T|               FADE IN:
O|
S|               NIGHT SEQUENCE
O|
N,G|               Series of shots of various streets and buildings in the town 
N|               of Bedford Falls, somewhere in New York State. The streets 
N|               are deserted, and snow is falling. It is Christmas Eve. Over 
N|               the above scenes we hear voices praying:
O|
C,E|                                     GOWER'S VOICE
U|                         I owe everything to George Bailey. 
U|                         Help him, dear Father.
O|
C,E|                                     MARTINI'S VOICE
U|                         Joseph, Jesus and Mary. Help my friend 
U|                         Mr. Bailey.
O|
C,E|                                     MRS. BAILEY'S VOICE
U|                         Help my son George tonight.
O|
C,E|                                     BERT'S VOICE
U|                         He never thinks about himself, God; 
U|                         that's why he's in trouble.
O|
C,E|                                     ERNIE'S VOICE
U|                         George is a good guy. Give him a 
U|                         break, God.
O|
C,E|                                     MARY'S VOICE
U|                         I love him, dear Lord. Watch over 
U|                         him tonight.
O|
C,E|                                     JANIE'S VOICE
U|                         Please, God. Something's the matter 
U|                         with Daddy.
O|
C,E|                                     ZUZU'S VOICE
U|                         Please bring Daddy back.
O|
N,G|               CAMERA PULLS UP from the Bailey home and travels up through 
N|               the sky until it is above the falling snow and moving slowly 
N,G|               toward a firmament full of stars. As the camera stops we 
N|               hear the following heavenly voices talking, and as each voice 
N|               is heard, one of the stars twinkles brightly:
O|
C,E|                                     FRANKLIN'S VOICE
U|                         Hello, Joseph, trouble?
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         Looks like we'll have to send someone 
U|                         down  a lot of people are asking 
U|                         for help for a man named George 
U|                         Bailey.
O|
C,E|                                     FRANKLIN'S VOICE
U|                         George Bailey. Yes, tonight's his 
U|                         crucial night. You're right, we'll 
U|                         have to send someone down immediately. 
U|                         Whose turn is it?
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         That's why I came to see you, sir. 
U|                         It's that clock-maker's turn again.
O|
C,E|                                     FRANKLIN'S VOICE
U|                         Oh  Clarence. Hasn't got his wings 
U|                         yet, has he? We've passed him up 
U|                         right along.
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         Because, you know, sir, he's got the 
U|                         I.Q. of a rabbit.
O|
C,E|                                     FRANKLIN'S VOICE
U|                         Yes, but he's got the faith of a 
U|                         child  simple. Joseph, send for 
U|                         Clarence.
O|
N|               A small star flies in from left of screen and stops. It 
N|               twinkles as Clarence speaks:
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         You sent for me, sir?
O|
C,E|                                     FRANKLIN'S VOICE
U|                         Yes, Clarence. A man down on earth 
U|                         needs our help.
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Splendid! Is he sick?
O|
C,E|                                     FRANKLIN'S VOICE
U|                         No, worse. He's discouraged. At 
U|                         exactly ten-forty-five PM tonight, 
U|                         Earth time, that man will be thinking 
U|                         seriously of throwing away God's 
U|                         greatest gift.
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Oh, dear, dear! His life! Then I've 
U|                         only got an hour to dress. What are 
U|                         they wearing now?
O|
C,E|                                     FRANKLIN'S VOICE
U|                         You will spend that hour getting 
U|                         acquainted with George Bailey.
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Sir... If I should accomplish this 
U|                         mission  I mean  might I perhaps 
U|                         win my wings?  I've been waiting for 
U|                         over two hundred years now, sir  
U|                         and people are beginning to talk.
O|
C,E|                                     FRANKLIN'S VOICE
U|                         What's that book you've got there?
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         The Adventures of Tom Sawyer.
O|
C,E|                                     FRANKLIN'S VOICE
U|                         Clarence, you do a good job with 
U|                         George Bailey, and you'll get your 
U|                         wings.
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Oh, thank you, sir. Thank you.
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         Poor George... Sit down.
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Sit down? What are...
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         If you're going to help a man, you 
U|                         want to know something about him, 
U|                         don't you?
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Well, naturally. Of course.
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         Well, keep your eyes open. See the 
U|                         town?
O|
N,G|               The stars fade out from the screen, and a light, 
N,G|               indistinguishable blur is seen.
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Where? I don't see a thing.
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         Oh, I forgot. You haven't got your 
U|                         wings yet. Now look, I'll help you 
U|                         out.  Concentrate. Begin to see 
U|                         something?
O|
N,G|               The blur on the screen slowly begins to take form. We see a 
N,G|               group of young boys on top of a snow-covered hill.
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Why, yes. This is amazing.
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         If you ever get your wings, you'll 
U|                         see all by yourself.
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Oh, wonderful!
O|
S,G|               EXT. FROZEN RIVER AND HILL  DAY  CLOSE SHOT
O|
N|               Group of boys. They are preparing to slide down the hill on 
N|               large shovels. One of them makes the slide and shoots out 
N|               onto the ice of a frozen river at the bottom of the hill.
O|
C|                                     BOY
P|                              (as he slides)
U|                         Yippee!!
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
U|                         Hey, who's that?
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         That's your problem, George Bailey.
O|
C,E|                                     CLARENCE'S VOICE
