O|
N|               On top of hill, preparing to make his slide.
O|
C|                                     HARRY
U|                         I'm not scared.
O|
C|                                     BOYS
P|                              (ad lib)
U|                         Come on, Harry! Attaboy, Harry!
O|
G|               MEDIUM SHOT
O|
N|               Harry makes his slide very fast. He passes the marks made by 
N|               the other boys, and his shovel takes him onto the thin ice 
N|               at the bend of the river. The ice breaks, and Harry disappears 
N|               into the water.
O|
G|               CLOSE SHOT  GEORGE
O|
C|                                     GEORGE
U|                         I'm coming, Harry.
O|
G|               MEDIUM SHOT
O|
N|               George jumps into the water and grabs Harry. As he starts to 
N|               pull him out he yells:
O|
C|                                     GEORGE
U|                         Make a chain, gang! A chain!
O|
G|               WIDER ANGLE
O|
N|               The other boys lie flat on the ice, forming a human chain. 
N|               When George reaches the edge with Harry in his arms, they 
N|               pull them both to safety.
O|
C,E|                                     JOSEPH'S VOICE
U|                         George saved his brother's life that 
U|                         day.  But he caught a bad cold which 
U|                         infected his left ear. Cost him his 
