S|               INT. BAILEY'S PRIVATE OFFICE  DAY
O|
G|               MEDIUM SHOT
O|
N|               George's father is seated behind his desk, nervously drawing 
N|               swirls on a pad. He looks tired and worried. He is a gentle 
N|               man in his forties, an idealist, stubborn only for other 
N|               people's rights.  Nearby, in a throne-like wheelchair, behind 
N|               which stands the goon who furnishes the motive power, sits 
N|               Henry F. Potter, his squarish derby hat on his head. The 
N|               following dialogue is fast and heated, as though the argument 
N|               had been in process for some time.
O|
